} {"question" "q-327163" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To calculate the $x$-intercepts, we need to substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the ellipse and solve the resulting equation for $x.$ We do this and solve the resulting equation by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}-20x+16y+20 & =0 \\\\ 5{x}^{2}+4\\cdot {0}^{2}-20x+16\\cdot 0+20 & =0 \\\\ 5{x}^{2}-20x+20 & =0 \\\\ 5\\,[{x}^{2}-4x]+20 & =0 \\\\ 5[(x-2)^{2}-4]+20 & =0 \\\\ 5(x-2)^{2}-20+20 & =0 \\\\ 5(x-2)^{2} & =0 \\\\ x-2 & =0 \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ellipse intercepts the $x$-axis at  $(2,0).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043117/state.json" "file_sha256" "df582b5d39f369aa387af1def6a4d18679d739a99c6f2e2e4589e4b7a026ec82"} {"question" "q-327163" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043117/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f0616c027bd3fc737991598e69577236f22ca130980f54841042acf71eb8364b"} {"question" "q-327163" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043117/state.json" "file_sha256" "df582b5d39f369aa387af1def6a4d18679d739a99c6f2e2e4589e4b7a026ec82"} {"question" "q-327163" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043117/state.json" "file_sha256" "df582b5d39f369aa387af1def6a4d18679d739a99c6f2e2e4589e4b7a026ec82"} {"question" "q-327163" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference